#: ../../source/api_reference/configurations.rst:96
msgid "Lazy Memory Allocator Configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_reference/configurations.rst:98
msgid ""
"Settings for the lazy memory allocator that enables gradual memory "
"allocation to reduce startup time and initial memory footprint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_reference/configurations.rst:102
msgid ""
"The lazy memory allocator is designed for scenarios with large CPU memory"
" configurations. It starts with a small initial allocation and gradually "
"expands as needed, reducing startup wait time and avoiding unnecessary "
"memory consumption when the full capacity is not required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_reference/configurations.rst:104
msgid "**Key characteristics:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_reference/configurations.rst:106
msgid ""
"**One-time expansion**: Memory expands until target size is reached, then"
" stops"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_reference/configurations.rst:107
msgid ""
"**No shrinking**: Once allocated, memory is never released back to the "
"system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_reference/configurations.rst:108
msgid ""
"**Automatic activation**: Only activates when ``max_local_cpu_size`` "
"exceeds ``lazy_memory_safe_size``"
msgstr ""

